  "description": "The \u0027potentially_problem_datasets\u0027 dataset is designed to help identify and manage datasets that may have issues or require special attention. It includes a variety of metadata about each dataset, such as its name, project association, existence status, and access URL. This dataset is particularly useful for data administrators and project managers who need to keep track of datasets across different projects, ensuring they are accessible, properly managed, and up-to-date. Key features include the ability to link datasets to specific projects via the \u0027projectKey\u0027, track dataset existence with the \u0027exists\u0027 column, and provide access details through the \u0027dataset_url\u0027. Additionally, it includes information about the dataset\u0027s storage type, format, and connection parameters, which are crucial for understanding how data is stored and accessed. The dataset also tracks modification history, including who last modified the dataset and when, which is essential for maintaining data integrity and accountability. Overall, this dataset serves as a comprehensive tool for managing datasets within an organization, ensuring they are properly documented and maintained.",
